## 1.4 Design-system contract

Centralize and document:

- Brand, semantic, text, surface, border, feedback and disabled-state colours.
- Font families, font weights, typography scale, line heights and heading hierarchy.
- Spacing, container widths, breakpoints and responsive layout rules.
- Border radii, shadows, overlays, stacking order and focus-ring styles.
- Motion duration, easing, distance, delay and reduced-motion behaviour.
- Standard states for hover, active, focus-visible, disabled, loading, error and success.
- Consistent form fields, buttons, cards, tabs, dialogs, drawers, sheets, toasts, skeletons and navigation surfaces.

Choose the actual font stack only after inspecting available font assets, current loading and build constraints. Do not invent font files or add a network-dependent font-loading requirement that makes production builds unreliable. Use a verified, properly licensed font source and a sensible fallback stack.

All shared CSS modules should consume the same design tokens. Audit existing hard-coded navy, blue-grey, gold and other colour values. Replace them only when they conflict with the approved system; preserve meaningful status colours.

## 1.5 Motion behaviour

| Interaction | Expected behaviour |
|---|---|
| Buttons and chips | Subtle colour, border and press transitions |
| Property cards | Restrained lift, shadow and image zoom |
| Mega menus | Smooth opacity and short vertical movement |
| Modals and drawers | Controlled fade/slide without abrupt appearance |
| Selected content sections | Optional subtle reveal; no compulsory animation on every element |
| Loading states | Calm skeleton pulse without distracting shimmer |
| Reduced motion | Disable or substantially reduce nonessential motion |

Rules:

- CSS-first motion; do not add a heavy animation dependency without demonstrated need.
- No layout jumps or animation-dependent functionality.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Keep keyboard focus clearly visible.
- Avoid unnecessary animation on large listing collections.
- Ensure motion styles are actually imported and applied.
- Do not add `MotionReveal` to every page indiscriminately.

## 1.6 Integration requirements

- Inspect `layout.tsx`, `globals.css`, tokens, base styles and foundation styles before editing.
- Preserve `AppShell`, `ErrorBoundary`, `ProductionQualityMonitor`, metadata and existing global imports.
- Integrate motion CSS through the canonical global style entry point.
- Ensure shared component class names and CSS Module classes remain compatible.
- Update `package.json` and lockfile together only when dependencies or scripts genuinely change.
- Preserve the existing `verify:foundation`, feature verifiers, authentication verifier, typecheck, lint and build workflow.
- Add `verify:design-system` only if the new verifier is implemented and its command is correct.

## 1.7 Part 1 PASS criteria

